                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I want to start with the positives.  Graphically this game is Beautiful, especially for being brought out in 2017.  The Ambient Sounds and Voice Acting? Truly good.  Nobody felt like they didn't understand the assignment and came across as wooden.   The puzzles? Sometimes quite thought provoking.   Some of them took a beat or two for me to get but as a veteran of Myst and it's Sequels i'm pretty well versed in this style of gameplay.   \n\nThese are all great qualities.  So what's the catch?   It breaks.  Frequently.  The game literally breaks and crashed and at that point why bother playing ti?  I'm totally over it.",
